WEBVTT

00:01.427 --> 00:04.417
<i>(SINGING) It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.862 --> 00:07.887
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.197 --> 00:11.596
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.865 --> 00:14.331
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:14.866 --> 00:17.425
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.168 --> 00:21.430
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:21.535 --> 00:23.024
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.136 --> 00:24.762
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:24.870 --> 00:29.635
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:38.276 --> 00:40.038
- Morning, Peter.
- Morning, Lois.

00:40.410 --> 00:42.172
- You using the bathroom?
- Yeah. Why?

00:42.277 --> 00:44.937
I was just curious. Before you go,
I want to ask you a question.

00:45.045 --> 00:46.808
Is there something on my elbow or...

00:46.913 --> 00:48.243
First, me first, me first.

00:54.316 --> 00:55.612
Peter, I'm going first!

00:55.716 --> 00:57.650
- Oh, no, you don't!
- Move your ass, Peter!

00:57.750 --> 01:00.149
- You move yours!
- I made reservations with the maоtre d'.

01:00.252 --> 01:01.616
Isn't that right, Cornelius?

01:01.752 --> 01:04.412
- Lois Griffin, poop for one.
- I also need a poop.

01:04.520 --> 01:07.215
- Do you have a reservation, sir?
- Yeah, I called a couple days ago.

01:07.322 --> 01:08.288
Who did you speak to?

01:08.388 --> 01:10.651
Dave... Al...

01:11.156 --> 01:14.851
Jeff... Ilium... Tonio?

01:14.958 --> 01:17.949
Dave-Al-Jeff-Ilium-Tonio
hasn't worked here for four years.

01:18.060 --> 01:20.049
The hell with you.
I'll use the other bathroom.

01:21.594 --> 01:22.685
MALE VOICE: Somebody's in here.

01:24.194 --> 01:25.490
Oh. Excuse me.

01:26.229 --> 01:27.218
Good morning?

01:27.797 --> 01:30.229
Lois, since when does
an elephant live here?

01:30.331 --> 01:33.025
LOIS: He's an exchange student.
Don't you remember?

01:33.131 --> 01:34.324
Oh, that's right.

01:34.432 --> 01:37.491
- Don't you feel foolish.
- Well, how long does it usually take you?

01:37.601 --> 01:40.727
- I don't remember.
- Oh, my God! That is such a bunch of crap.

01:40.835 --> 01:43.267
I hope my son is having a better time
with your family.

01:43.369 --> 01:44.562
(SCREAMING)

01:44.669 --> 01:46.158
Poachers!

01:48.239 --> 01:49.637
(WHIMPERING)

01:52.306 --> 01:54.535
- Joe, I need to use your bathroom.
- Sure, Peter.

01:58.142 --> 02:00.574
What the hell? How do you even...

02:01.577 --> 02:03.372
What? It... I don't...

02:04.812 --> 02:06.369
Wait. How do I...

02:06.479 --> 02:08.844
JOE: Yeah. That's gonna be
way too complicated for you.

02:08.947 --> 02:11.743
- How come there are two toilets?
- The other one's for blood.

02:12.915 --> 02:14.677
(WHIMPERING)

02:17.551 --> 02:19.142
Cleveland's old house. Perfect!

02:22.019 --> 02:23.315
Damn, no toilet paper.

02:25.120 --> 02:26.916
- Hey, Joe, can I borrow this?
- JOE: Sure.

02:34.123 --> 02:35.249
Peter, where have you been?

02:35.358 --> 02:39.417
Let's just say I've been at Cleveland's
empty house taking a dump.

02:39.526 --> 02:41.083
(GROANING) That's disgusting.

02:41.194 --> 02:44.786
I will be taking all of my movements there
from now on. All of them!

02:44.895 --> 02:46.328
(EX CLAIMING)

02:46.429 --> 02:48.521
<i>(LET'S GETLOUD PLAYING)</i>

02:48.631 --> 02:50.824
<i>Let's get loud, let's get loud</i>

02:50.931 --> 02:55.797
<i>Turn the music up, let's do it
Come on, people, let's get loud</i>

02:55.900 --> 02:57.696
<i>Let's get loud</i>

02:58.234 --> 03:01.292
<i>Turn the music up to hear that sound</i>

03:01.402 --> 03:02.834
<i>Let's get loud</i>

03:08.171 --> 03:09.535
Peter, your breakfast is ready.

03:09.639 --> 03:12.037
Hang on, I'll be right back, Lois.
I'm just going across the street.

03:12.139 --> 03:14.629
Peter, you can't keep
using Cleveland's bathroom.

03:14.741 --> 03:16.333
Oh, my God. Yes, I can.

03:16.441 --> 03:18.340
Cleveland's bathroom
is the greatest discovery

03:18.442 --> 03:20.466
since fat women discovered Diet Coke.

03:22.310 --> 03:24.004
Now I can eat anything!

03:28.855 --> 03:31.651
Hey, hey, hey. No, no, no.
What are you doing? That's my bathroom!

03:31.756 --> 03:33.723
What are you talking about?
We just rented this place.

03:34.357 --> 03:37.382
Holy crap! Dan Aykroyd and Chevy Chase!

03:37.492 --> 03:39.550
What the hell are you guys
doing in Quahog?

03:39.660 --> 03:41.785
We're just doing research for a movie.

03:41.893 --> 03:43.382
Oh, my God, that's amazing.

03:43.494 --> 03:44.551
Listen, I got to tell you guys,

03:44.661 --> 03:47.060
I've watched all your movies,
like, 1,000 times.

03:47.162 --> 03:49.721
<i>- You saw Cops and Robbersons?
- And My Stepmother is an Alien?</i>

03:49.831 --> 03:50.819
Almost all of them.

03:50.931 --> 03:54.023
Boy, I sure would love it if you guys would
come to our house for dinner tonight.

03:54.132 --> 03:56.497
My wife's cooking sucks,
but I just want to look at you.

03:56.600 --> 03:58.624
- You like meatloaf?
- Yeah. Sure.

03:58.734 --> 04:00.133
All right, see you at 8:00.

04:00.234 --> 04:03.633
<i>Man, I can't believe I'm gonna have dinner
with two of the Three Amigos!</i>

04:03.736 --> 04:04.963
This is gonna be way better
than when we had

04:05.069 --> 04:07.469
that Victorian girl ghost over for dinner.

04:07.704 --> 04:08.762
(MUSIC BOX TINKLING)

04:08.872 --> 04:11.270
(CRYING) My governess drowned me
in a well.

04:12.072 --> 04:13.800
You are a horrible dinner guest.

04:19.242 --> 04:22.676
<i>Can you believe it? We're eating
with two of the three Ghostbusters.</i>

04:22.777 --> 04:23.970
Actually, I wasn't in that.

04:24.077 --> 04:26.307
Look at these guys!
They can't take a compliment!

04:26.413 --> 04:30.107
You know, you guys are funny,
but I got a confession to make.

04:30.647 --> 04:32.840
I'm a pretty funny guy myself.

04:32.948 --> 04:34.915
Maybe I say a few things here,
maybe I get a few laughs,

04:35.015 --> 04:36.642
maybe you guys put me
in one of your pictures.

04:36.750 --> 04:39.081
Well, yeah, I suppose it's possible.

04:39.184 --> 04:41.014
Yeah, we've got all kinds of roles available.

04:41.118 --> 04:43.779
Speaking roles, background roles.
Background would be good for you.

04:43.886 --> 04:46.217
Yeah. Speaking role or background role,
either one would be good.

04:46.321 --> 04:48.083
You know, I'm really good at sight gags.

04:48.788 --> 04:50.778
Oh! I didn't mean to do that.

04:50.889 --> 04:52.787
Now it's everywhere!

04:52.889 --> 04:53.913
That's comedy.

04:54.023 --> 04:54.989
(STEWIE LAUGHING)

04:55.090 --> 04:57.489
Peter, what the hell is wrong with you?
That's not funny.

04:57.592 --> 04:59.252
Oh, well, interesting opinion, Lois.

04:59.359 --> 05:00.985
Gee, I wonder if
there's anyone else at this table

05:01.093 --> 05:03.855
who's maybe more qualified to say
what's funny than you are.

05:03.961 --> 05:05.951
Well, we'd need to see
a little bit more, but...

05:06.062 --> 05:07.120
(LAUGHING)

05:07.230 --> 05:09.719
Is that the time?
I can't believe that's the time. It's late.

05:10.497 --> 05:12.794
What? I don't understand.
You're not wearing a watch.

05:12.898 --> 05:14.887
Well, you see, that's sort of a joke, Peter.

05:15.699 --> 05:18.826
- Oh. Well, that's not that funny.
- It's kind of funny, you know.

05:18.934 --> 05:21.025
No, it's not funny.
See, if you had said something like,

05:21.135 --> 05:22.567
"It's half past a freckle."

05:22.668 --> 05:23.656
(LAUGHING)

05:23.769 --> 05:26.498
You know, I'm thinking,
of the three of you,

05:26.604 --> 05:28.764
I'm... I'm thinking this guy.

05:28.872 --> 05:30.031
Let me show you something that's funny.

05:30.172 --> 05:33.162
Okay, here's an impression of John Wayne
on the first Thanksgiving.

05:33.573 --> 05:37.439
"I'm John Wayne
at the first Thanksgiving, pilgrims.

05:37.542 --> 05:39.906
"Happy Thanksgiving, pilgrims!"

05:40.109 --> 05:41.541
(LAUGHING)

05:41.643 --> 05:42.870
Where's this guy been?

05:42.977 --> 05:45.035
Well, Mr. Griffin, this has been a lot of fun.

05:45.145 --> 05:47.135
- A lot of fun.
- But we got to get back over to our place

05:47.246 --> 05:50.179
and kind of do... What do we have to do?

05:50.280 --> 05:52.543
- Roll some joints and get high.
- Yeah, we got to do those things.

05:52.647 --> 05:54.705
That's not funny. Drugs aren't funny.

05:55.015 --> 05:57.006
- They ruin lives.
- Amen.

05:57.116 --> 05:59.913
- No, Peter. You're not funny.
- I'm afraid Dan's right.

06:00.017 --> 06:02.314
- You're not funny at all.
- I don't get it.

06:02.419 --> 06:03.715
You're painfully unfunny.

06:04.419 --> 06:05.386
Get the (BLEEP) out of my house!

06:10.399 --> 06:11.797
Hey, Stewie, can I talk to you for a sec?

06:11.899 --> 06:14.730
Look, Brian,
I've colored Sebastian the crab blue!

06:15.067 --> 06:18.558
If that isn't a middle finger to society,
I don't know what is.

06:19.436 --> 06:22.062
I don't like it anymore.
I wish I'd colored him red.

06:22.170 --> 06:23.159
Do you think it's a little odd

06:23.271 --> 06:26.830
that Chevy Chase and Dan Aykroyd
have moved into Quahog together?

06:26.939 --> 06:28.667
I mean, why here? Why now?

06:28.774 --> 06:31.240
I don't know.
Maybe we go over there and find out.

06:31.341 --> 06:32.398
Maybe we do.

06:32.508 --> 06:36.636
Hey. Hi, there. Can you guys tell Meg
I'm seeing someone?

06:40.111 --> 06:42.703
- BRIAN: You see anything?
- Doesn't look like anybody's home.

06:42.812 --> 06:43.835
(GUNS COCKING)

06:46.314 --> 06:48.439
Won't you gentlemen have a Pepsi?

06:57.819 --> 07:02.082
- What do we do?
- "Won't you gentlemen have a Pepsi?"

07:06.890 --> 07:08.117
(BOTH SCREAMING)

07:12.425 --> 07:14.085
- Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
- Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

07:14.192 --> 07:15.590
Yell, yell, yell. Yell, yell, yell.

07:24.708 --> 07:27.642
What the... What the hell is this place?

07:27.744 --> 07:28.711
Welcome to DUMP,

07:28.811 --> 07:31.073
Deep Underground
Military Protection Facility.

07:31.178 --> 07:34.634
- Wouldn't that be DUMPF?
- The "F" is silent, like in "knife."

07:34.747 --> 07:37.738
We're actually working for the federal
government, and we need your help.

07:37.848 --> 07:39.678
Do you want to be spies like us?

07:39.782 --> 07:41.248
Can we be spies like them?

07:41.750 --> 07:43.875
We've actually resolved our differences.

07:50.887 --> 07:52.046
Wait a minute. I don't understand.

07:52.154 --> 07:53.983
What do you mean
you guys work for the government?

07:54.087 --> 07:57.578
<i>Well, Brian, it turns out Spies Like Us
was Ronald Reagan's favorite movie,</i>

07:57.690 --> 08:01.021
so he actually appointed us
honorary spies back in the '80s.

08:01.125 --> 08:03.057
That still doesn't explain
what you're doing here.

08:03.158 --> 08:04.556
You see, Brian, during the Cold War,

08:04.658 --> 08:07.217
the Soviet Union brainwashed
dozens of American civilians,

08:07.327 --> 08:08.918
effectively making them sleeper agents

08:09.027 --> 08:12.017
who could be activated at anytime
to do the work of the KGB.

08:12.229 --> 08:13.195
Activated how?

08:13.295 --> 08:16.320
The agents could be activated
by uttering a predetermined phrase.

08:16.431 --> 08:18.057
At which point,
they would snap into a trance

08:18.165 --> 08:22.223
and mindlessly carry out whatever orders
they were given by their KGB handlers.

08:22.333 --> 08:24.129
Well, I mean,
what if they encountered somebody

08:24.234 --> 08:26.326
- who said the phrase accidentally?
- Not possible.

08:26.435 --> 08:29.527
The activation phrase was something
that no one would ever think to utter.

08:29.636 --> 08:31.102
- What is it?
- The phrase is,

08:31.203 --> 08:34.500
"Gosh, that Italian family at the next table
sure is quiet."

08:34.904 --> 08:37.304
You see, the U.S. Government believes
that one of these sleeper agents

08:37.407 --> 08:38.498
is right here in Quahog.

08:38.607 --> 08:41.005
Now, you two individuals live here.

08:41.107 --> 08:44.040
Are there any local residents
whom you've seen acting strangely?

08:44.142 --> 08:45.472
Well, there's a pedophile up the street

08:45.576 --> 08:47.099
that nobody seems to be
doing anything about,

08:47.210 --> 08:48.733
but it's mainly because he's so funny.

08:48.844 --> 08:51.106
Well, look, we'd be happy to
help in any way we can.

08:51.211 --> 08:53.075
Hey, is Ron Howard's
weird-Iooking brother

08:53.179 --> 08:54.475
one of these lab technicians?

08:54.579 --> 08:56.342
Of course he is. It's an '80s movie.

08:56.680 --> 08:58.340
Hey, there's something on the screen.

09:02.482 --> 09:05.348
And those two bums turned to me
and said, "You're not funny, Peter."

09:05.450 --> 09:07.577
- In my own house!
- Well, what was the bit?

09:07.685 --> 09:08.673
Okay, ready?

09:08.786 --> 09:12.776
I'm John Wayne
at the first Thanksgiving, pilgrims.

09:12.887 --> 09:15.377
Happy Thanksgiving, pilgrims.

09:15.489 --> 09:17.387
(LAUGHING)

09:17.489 --> 09:18.614
- Oh, God.
- Oh, my.

09:18.723 --> 09:19.883
Oh, my God, Peter!

09:19.991 --> 09:22.890
I'll tell you, and I'm your friend
and I'll be honest with you, that's funny.

09:22.991 --> 09:23.980
That is funny.

09:24.092 --> 09:26.559
And you know what I appreciate
about your joke, Peter?

09:26.660 --> 09:28.752
It's clean. It's clean funny!

09:28.894 --> 09:31.453
I just wish there was some way
I could show them how wrong they are.

09:31.562 --> 09:33.357
Show them that we know comedy
better than they do.

09:33.462 --> 09:34.554
Hey, I got an idea.

09:34.662 --> 09:38.119
What's the most consistently funny form
of comedy in existence?

09:39.465 --> 09:40.863
- Improv?
- Improv!

09:40.965 --> 09:42.488
- Improv!
- Improv!

09:42.599 --> 09:44.225
- Improv!
- Improv!

09:44.900 --> 09:46.232
We'll start our own improv group
and put on a show.

09:46.334 --> 09:47.301
All right!

09:52.077 --> 09:54.236
Thank you for seeing us
on such short notice, Mayor West.

09:54.344 --> 09:55.777
No problem, gentlemen.

09:55.879 --> 09:58.345
- May I call you "gentlemen"?
- Yeah.

09:58.446 --> 10:01.811
Now, you say this spy is located
somewhere in Quahog?

10:01.915 --> 10:05.144
That's right. We need you to set up
some roadblocks to help us contain him.

10:05.249 --> 10:08.239
Do you have any clues
regarding the identity of the spy?

10:08.350 --> 10:09.442
It's a little tricky, sir.

10:09.552 --> 10:12.348
See, the operative is completely unaware
that he's been programmed,

10:12.452 --> 10:13.645
and the only way to activate him

10:13.753 --> 10:16.380
and discover his identity
is by saying the phrase,

10:16.488 --> 10:20.148
"Gosh, that Italian family at the next table
sure is quiet!"

10:20.255 --> 10:21.222
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

10:24.657 --> 10:25.817
It's him!

10:39.463 --> 10:40.486
(BEEPING)

10:44.399 --> 10:45.491
(MOANING)

10:45.600 --> 10:49.624
I haven't been this... Since I...

10:53.336 --> 10:58.794
I don't... I don't really know
what I'm supposed to be doing, but...

10:59.471 --> 11:01.267
Oh, there's track star Wilma Rudolph.

11:01.806 --> 11:04.136
Obviously, she had something to do
with the gag,

11:04.774 --> 11:09.141
but I didn't hear the setup,
so I don't really know the context...

11:09.243 --> 11:10.607
Hey, I wonder what Peter's up to!

11:14.077 --> 11:16.204
Okay, so we got to come up with
a name for our improv group.

11:16.313 --> 11:18.246
- Anybody got anything?
- BOTH: Um...

11:18.713 --> 11:21.407
- How about the Jokeridge Boys?
- Not bad.

11:21.514 --> 11:25.540
- Wait. How about Funny Side Up?
- No, no, no. Guys, guys, we got the name.

11:25.649 --> 11:28.878
It's Improv-de-Colon-
the-Truth-is-Ad Libbed.

11:29.218 --> 11:33.345
- What about Deliveries in Rear?
- Oh, yes!

11:33.452 --> 11:36.181
No, no! No, you can't just jam jokes in
for no reason!

11:36.287 --> 11:38.049
It has to be organic to the situation!

11:38.155 --> 11:40.485
What the hell you being
so frigging comedy Hitler about?

11:40.589 --> 11:42.852
I was in three improv groups
in college, Peter.

11:42.957 --> 11:45.982
I was in Improvidence,
I was in the Wackadamia Nuts,

11:46.091 --> 11:48.615
and I know I'm dating myself here,
but Three Smile Island.

11:48.726 --> 11:51.557
My point being that I am the only
experienced member of this group.

11:51.794 --> 11:53.817
I can already tell this is not gonna be fun.

12:06.133 --> 12:07.394
How do we know where to start looking?

12:07.500 --> 12:09.262
The tracking beacon I shot
into Mayor West's ankle

12:09.368 --> 12:10.800
will allow us to locate him.

12:15.337 --> 12:17.463
Wow. Those are the Russian people?

12:19.705 --> 12:21.831
I mean, granted,
you do think of bears on unicycles

12:21.939 --> 12:25.396
when you think of the Russian people,
but they're all bears on unicycles?

12:25.507 --> 12:26.996
Bears on unicycles, every one.

12:27.108 --> 12:28.132
So what do we do now?

12:28.243 --> 12:30.937
We're undercover U.S. Agents
in a hostile foreign territory.

12:31.043 --> 12:33.703
We just got to make sure we don't
do anything that makes us stick out.

12:33.811 --> 12:35.801
Hey, they're not bears on unicycles!

12:38.180 --> 12:41.375
- You are under arrest.
- Time to lose this costume.

12:43.214 --> 12:44.942
(LAUGHING) 'Cause we're in Russia!

12:55.523 --> 12:58.922
Here are the American spies we captured,
Mr. Prime Minister.

13:01.825 --> 13:02.791
(GASPING)

13:04.192 --> 13:05.420
(SIGHING)

13:06.761 --> 13:07.920
(GASPING)

13:10.396 --> 13:11.362
(SIGHING)

13:13.230 --> 13:14.389
(GASPING)

13:15.598 --> 13:16.723
(SIGHING)

13:16.965 --> 13:19.898
He was "Putin" us on, huh? Right?

13:19.999 --> 13:22.488
What do you think of that? Chevy?

13:22.600 --> 13:26.160
Right? That would have passed for funny
in one of your movies, right?

13:26.269 --> 13:27.292
Okay, moving on.

13:27.403 --> 13:31.359
Gentlemen, let me put your minds at ease.
I know why you are here,

13:31.470 --> 13:32.959
and I mean to help you.

13:33.071 --> 13:34.469
(LAUGHING)

13:34.571 --> 13:35.936
Well, terrific.

13:36.040 --> 13:39.337
The truth is the reactivation
of a Cold War sleeper spy

13:39.441 --> 13:41.566
would be an embarrassment
to my government.

13:41.675 --> 13:45.474
On the scale of our 1981 failed
Czechoslovakian occupation outpost,

13:45.577 --> 13:47.406
which was penetrated by Bill Murray,

13:47.511 --> 13:50.444
Harold Ramis,
and their ragtag band of misfit soldiers

13:50.545 --> 13:51.909
who didn't even graduate!

13:52.012 --> 13:54.570
They slept through
the graduation ceremony and somehow

13:54.680 --> 13:58.308
managed to come out of the manhole
wearing clean, pressed suit, as you say.

13:58.416 --> 14:01.542
So the long and the veiny of it is,
you're gonna help us out, right?

14:01.650 --> 14:05.550
I will provide you with transportation,
passports, food, supplies,

14:05.652 --> 14:08.084
everything from "A" to backwards "R."

14:08.186 --> 14:10.483
Wow! Thank you so much for your help,
Mr. Putin.

14:10.587 --> 14:12.610
Would you like to see
Russian cutaway gag?

14:12.721 --> 14:15.211
- Yeah, sure.
- Here is Russian cutaway gag.

14:15.456 --> 14:17.423
(EX CLAIMING IN RUSSIAN)

14:24.693 --> 14:26.058
(LAUGHING)

14:29.395 --> 14:30.861
Where the hell is Quagmire?

14:30.962 --> 14:33.190
I don't know.
He said improv rehearsal at 7:00, right?

14:33.296 --> 14:35.525
Yeah, where is Quagmire?
I haven't seen him all day.

14:35.631 --> 14:37.860
You know what?
I think he went down to the bank.

14:38.799 --> 14:39.958
What was that? What did you hit me for?

14:40.066 --> 14:42.590
I'm passing the story on to you.
Keep it going. Keep the story going.

14:42.701 --> 14:44.031
- Huh?
- What's Quagmire doing at the bank?

14:44.134 --> 14:45.226
It's improv, Peter. You don't think.

14:45.335 --> 14:46.961
You don't think.
You just keep talking. You don't think.

14:47.070 --> 14:48.161
Don't think. Don't think.
What comes to mind?

14:48.270 --> 14:49.236
Talk, talk, talk, talk, talk!

14:49.336 --> 14:51.734
I get it. Tap me, Quagmire, tap me!

14:51.837 --> 14:55.363
Quagmire went to the bank to donate
sperm because it's a sperm bank.

14:55.473 --> 14:56.939
Yes, there you go. He's moving it forward.

14:57.040 --> 14:59.063
He's moving it forward. See, Peter?
Now tap Peter.

15:00.041 --> 15:03.769
Hey, pilgrims.
Happy Thanksgiving, pilgrims.

15:03.909 --> 15:05.638
It's me, John Wayne.

15:05.744 --> 15:07.642
Oh, no. All right, you know what?
You're not loosened up yet.

15:07.744 --> 15:09.711
All right, let's do some warm-up exercises.

15:09.812 --> 15:12.870
Okay, this is one we call
"Going Bananas." Okay.

15:12.979 --> 15:15.742
<i>(SINGING) I'm a banana
I'm a banana</i>

15:16.182 --> 15:18.808
<i>Peel the banana
Peel the banana</i>

15:18.916 --> 15:22.111
<i>Now go bananas!
Go, go bananas!</i>

15:22.450 --> 15:24.417
<i>Go!</i>

15:25.118 --> 15:27.847
Come on, you guys. Do it with me.
Go bananas. Yeah!

15:27.953 --> 15:29.351
(SHOUTING)

15:30.554 --> 15:31.918
Whole body, Joe. Whole body.

15:32.887 --> 15:34.217
Come on. Go bananas.

15:35.056 --> 15:36.954
Am I doing it? Am I doing it?

15:37.056 --> 15:38.522
(BLEEP) the matter with you guys?

15:38.623 --> 15:40.954
All right, let's try something else.
Okay, this is a warm-up exercise

15:41.058 --> 15:42.614
called "One-Word Story."

15:42.725 --> 15:44.624
Now, I start a story with one word,

15:44.726 --> 15:47.387
and then you each continue
with one word at a time.

15:47.494 --> 15:49.358
- Okay, ready?
- Yeah, yeah. I'm into this now.

15:49.462 --> 15:52.054
- Okay. The...
- Dog...

15:52.162 --> 15:53.856
- And...
- My...

15:53.963 --> 15:55.953
- Mom...
- And...

15:56.064 --> 15:58.054
- This...
- Handkerchief...

15:58.165 --> 15:59.825
- And...
- Twenty...

15:59.933 --> 16:01.399
- Birds...
- And...

16:01.500 --> 16:02.830
- Peter.
- Geez.

16:02.934 --> 16:04.264
- And...
- Peter, hang on a sec.

16:04.367 --> 16:06.266
- You're not contributing.
- I'm doing it.

16:06.368 --> 16:07.766
You're not adding information.

16:07.869 --> 16:09.267
Well, one of you guys says "Thanksgiving,"

16:09.369 --> 16:12.461
- I got a good idea where to go with it.
- Okay, Peter, let's try something different.

16:13.304 --> 16:16.397
Okay, close your eyes.
What's the first thing you see?

16:16.506 --> 16:18.803
- Uh...
- Don't think, just say it. First thing.

16:18.907 --> 16:20.464
- Pelican.
- Okay, what's he doing?

16:20.575 --> 16:23.098
He's complaining
about some undercooked food.

16:23.209 --> 16:24.175
Who's he complaining to?

16:24.275 --> 16:28.141
A snooty French waiter
who's really mean to his customers.

16:28.244 --> 16:30.507
But then when he goes home,
his own life's sad

16:30.612 --> 16:34.010
because his girlfriend's mean to him,
and his apartment isn't so very nice,

16:34.113 --> 16:36.081
and he's always running out
of paper towels.

16:36.181 --> 16:37.670
(GASPING)

16:39.615 --> 16:43.743
I saw it... I seen it, Quagmire.
I was there in the apartment!

16:44.417 --> 16:45.406
We're ready.

16:48.886 --> 16:50.147
If these signatures are correct,

16:50.253 --> 16:53.084
Mayor West is located
one-third of a kilometer that way.

16:53.187 --> 16:54.244
Just over this rise.

16:54.354 --> 16:57.254
Yeah, that's what you told us
a third of a kilometer ago, you douche.

16:57.356 --> 16:59.220
Perhaps you'd like to do
something besides

16:59.324 --> 17:01.018
criticizing me and quoting my movies?

17:01.125 --> 17:02.421
You just watch your mouth, mister!

17:05.160 --> 17:06.387
Look!

17:11.929 --> 17:12.896
(GASPING)

17:22.467 --> 17:26.401
Anyway, I'd be happy to help you
conduct a search of Quahog and find...

17:26.502 --> 17:28.469
What the hell? Where am I?

17:28.570 --> 17:31.560
I didn't just bite into
a YORK peppermint patty, did I?

17:31.704 --> 17:32.727
Mayor West, you're in Russia.

17:32.838 --> 17:35.499
You've just launched a nuclear missile
against the United States.

17:35.606 --> 17:39.767
Well, this day has taken a bad turn,
like Mike Brady's first marriage.

17:40.575 --> 17:41.836
Here's your beer, honey.

17:44.610 --> 17:47.270
I don't remember asking for a warm beer.

17:47.378 --> 17:49.572
Well, I didn't want to quit working.
You made me.

17:49.678 --> 17:52.441
You don't talk to me that way!

17:54.714 --> 17:58.613
- Alice, what did you see?
- Enough to know I'm getting a raise.

18:08.620 --> 18:11.780
What the... Oh, man.
We're supposed to do a show tonight.

18:11.887 --> 18:14.411
Where's the audience?
I don't see them anywhere.

18:14.522 --> 18:16.921
If only they could make some noise
to let me know they're here.

18:17.024 --> 18:20.185
- MAN 1: We're here.
- Oh, there you are. Thank God.

18:20.292 --> 18:23.850
Well, we're Room for Improv-ment.
So without further ado, I need a place.

18:23.959 --> 18:26.324
- MAN 1: Your ass!
- Okay, come on now.

18:26.427 --> 18:28.519
- Something serious.
- MAN 1: Your mom's ass!

18:28.628 --> 18:31.356
Hey, let's get that guy out of here, huh?
Okay, a real place.

18:31.462 --> 18:33.553
MAN 2: Goldman's Pharmacy
on Third and Maple.

18:33.663 --> 18:34.722
WOMAN: Give them the hours.

18:34.831 --> 18:37.059
- MAN 2: 8:00 a.m. To...
- Okay, I heard "pharmacy."

18:37.165 --> 18:39.064
- Who's in the pharmacy?
- PETER: John Wayne!

18:39.166 --> 18:40.995
What the... Peter, you're not supposed
to be in the audience.

18:41.099 --> 18:42.497
Get the hell up onstage.

18:44.267 --> 18:47.167
All right. Hey there, sir.
Welcome to my pharmacy. Can I help you?

18:47.269 --> 18:49.701
Here's John Wayne
at the first Thanksgiving.

18:49.803 --> 18:52.396
"Happy Thanksgiving, pilgrims!"

18:52.504 --> 18:54.597
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

18:54.706 --> 18:58.140
You like that? Okay, here's John Wayne
Bobbitt at the first Thanksgiving.

18:58.574 --> 19:00.905
"Where's my penis, pilgrims?"

19:01.008 --> 19:03.031
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

19:03.142 --> 19:05.974
And here's John Wayne Gacy
at the first Thanksgiving.

19:06.311 --> 19:08.335
"I want to dress up like a clown

19:08.445 --> 19:11.741
"and have sex with children
and kill them, pilgrims."

19:11.845 --> 19:14.312
(AUDIENCE LAUGHING)

19:14.414 --> 19:19.906
- Guys, I got to split. I took a wet duke.
- And...

19:20.016 --> 19:22.073
Okay, this is not something that should
ever have been attempted.

19:22.183 --> 19:23.911
Thank you very much.
Good night, everybody.

19:24.017 --> 19:24.984
Improv!

19:40.058 --> 19:42.547
I wish there was some way
I could have prevented this.

19:42.658 --> 19:45.217
It wasn't your fault, Mayor West.
There's nothing you could have done.

19:45.327 --> 19:47.487
To be honest, I don't remember a thing,

19:47.595 --> 19:50.687
<i>except how much I love
the Michael Jackson Thriller video.</i>

19:50.796 --> 19:53.126
Boy, could that guy dance.

19:53.229 --> 19:57.095
Guy dance? Guidance!
Source programmable guidance!

19:57.198 --> 19:59.324
We can reprogram
and disarm the missile from here.

19:59.433 --> 20:02.093
From here? Well, our arms
would have to be 40-feet long, Dan.

20:02.200 --> 20:04.531
No, yutz, not from right here.
We go over there and do it.

20:04.635 --> 20:06.898
- Oh, right.
- Oh, come on, Chevy.

20:07.002 --> 20:09.265
You should have known
what he was talking about.

20:09.970 --> 20:12.801
All I have to do is bypass
the primary navigational-guidance circuits,

20:12.904 --> 20:16.134
deprogram the hardwired safety overrides,
and reconfigure the motherboard

20:16.239 --> 20:19.138
so that the missile's primary
central-processing unit tells itself

20:19.240 --> 20:23.037
to eject its own warhead while still
safely above the Earth's atmosphere.

20:23.375 --> 20:24.865
Hey, Dan, when this is all over,

20:24.977 --> 20:27.808
you may get a call asking you
to evaluate my performance.

20:27.911 --> 20:29.775
Can I count on you to give me a 10?

20:30.478 --> 20:31.910
And that should do it.

20:44.285 --> 20:46.478
You did it, Dan. My God, you did it!

20:46.585 --> 20:49.643
Yes. Oh, my God. You did it. You did it.

20:50.554 --> 20:53.146
Mission accomplished, gentlemen.
Warhead has been destroyed.

20:53.254 --> 20:54.585
We've saved millions of lives.

20:54.689 --> 20:57.918
Let's just hope the fuselage doesn't fall
where it can cause too much damage.

21:03.082 --> 21:06.050
No, no, no, no, no, no!

21:08.185 --> 21:09.515
I... I don't get it.

21:17.355 --> 21:20.413
So, what's the deal with Chris?
Is he actually, like, still in Africa?

21:20.523 --> 21:21.511
No, no, he's not.

21:21.623 --> 21:24.591
- So that was all... That was just a bit?
- Yeah, he'll be back next week.

21:24.691 --> 21:27.487
Great. Boy, who would have thought
all this trouble could be caused

21:27.592 --> 21:29.024
by simply uttering the phrase,

21:29.126 --> 21:32.355
"Gosh, that Italian family at the next table
sure is quiet."

21:38.764 --> 21:40.162
(SPEAKING RUSSIAN)

21:45.500 --> 21:47.592
<i>MAN: (WITH RUSSIAN ACCENT)
Shut up, 2476.</i>

21:47.593 --> 22:48.593
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru